{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 168620, "name": "Phillip Dudley", "username": "filbot3", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/filbot3/{size}/1769_2.png", "created_at": "2020-08-17T18:34:43.945Z", "cooked": "<p>I wanted to install Git Flow tooling for Fedora 32 Workstation. According to the documentation, I just need to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/nvie/gitflow/wiki/Linux#installing-on-fedora\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Linux · nvie/gitflow Wiki · GitHub</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>which says to just run:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\">sudo dnf install gitflow\nkeybase                                                10 kB/s | 3.3 kB     00:00\nNo match for argument: gitflow\nError: Unable to find a match: gitflow\n</code></pre>\n<p>However, when I run this, there is no package available for gitflow. I then looked around and saw some people said it was in the EPEL, which we’re not supposed to enable for Fedora, then others say to enable the RPM Fusion repositories, which those already are. Here is the list of enabled repos:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-bash\">sudo dnf repolist\n[sudo] password for filbot:\nrepo id                           repo name\ncode                              Visual Studio Code\nfedora                            Fedora 32 - x86_64\nfedora-cisco-openh264             Fedora 32 openh264 (From Cisco) - x86_64\nfedora-modular                    Fedora Modular 32 - x86_64\ngoogle-chrome                     google-chrome\nkeybase                           keybase\nkubernetes                        Kubernetes\nrpmfusion-free                    RPM Fusion for Fedora 32 - Free\nrpmfusion-free-updates            RPM Fusion for Fedora 32 - Free - Updates\nrpmfusion-nonfree                 RPM Fusion for Fedora 32 - Nonfree\nrpmfusion-nonfree-updates         RPM Fusion for Fedora 32 - Nonfree - Updates\nteams                             teams\nupdates                           Fedora 32 - x86_64 - Updates\nupdates-modular                   Fedora Modular 32 - x86_64 - Updates\n</code></pre>\n<p>What would I need to do to install the gitflow package via the dnf package manager? I could install via their script, but I would like it to be managed via dnf.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-06-22T17:00:46.561Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 4829, "reads": 44, "readers_count": 43, "score": 24153.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77964, "topic_slug": "unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already", "display_username": "Phillip Dudley", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 3, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://github.com/nvie/gitflow/wiki/Linux#installing-on-fedora", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Linux · nvie/gitflow Wiki · GitHub", "clicks": 126}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 1726, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already/77964/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 170414, "name": "Alessio", "username": "alciregi", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/alciregi/{size}/5506_2.png", "created_at": "2020-08-17T19:01:48.130Z", "cooked": "<p>Hello.<br>\nAs you can see, <a href=\"https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/gitflow\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Overview - rpms/gitflow - src.fedoraproject.org</a>, the package is orphaned. It was last packaged for Fedora 31.</p>\n<p>What happened? The package maintainer  stopped to maintain it. For which reason? We should search in the devel mailing list, usually the maintainers announce there their intention to stop the maintenance of some package. Then? Nobody else volunteers to take this work for gitflow, hence the package was orphaned and removed from the Fedora repository (for the subsequent releases).</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2020-08-17T19:01:48.130Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 25, "reads": 42, "readers_count": 41, "score": 213.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77964, "topic_slug": "unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already", "display_username": "Alessio", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/gitflow", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Overview - rpms/gitflow - src.fedoraproject.org", "clicks": 292}], "read": true, "user_title": "Speak Up!", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 3}], "moderator": true, "admin": false, "staff": true, "user_id": 109, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already/77964/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 3}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 3, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 141832, "name": "Phillip Dudley", "username": "filbot3", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/filbot3/{size}/1769_2.png", "created_at": "2020-08-17T23:10:03.441Z", "cooked": "<p>Which mailing lists do you generally look at? My Google-fu brings me to posts from 2015 and RPM Fusion a lot.</p>\n<p>So the package is unmaintained and not available. Thank you for the update. I will add that URL you shared earlier to my bookmarks and places to look.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2020-08-17T23:10:03.441Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 13, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 138.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77964, "topic_slug": "unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already", "display_username": "Phillip Dudley", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 8, "username": "miabbott", "name": "Micah Abbott", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/miabbott/{size}/11_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 1726, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already/77964/3", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 110778, "name": "Alessio", "username": "alciregi", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/alciregi/{size}/5506_2.png", "created_at": "2020-08-18T05:46:05.666Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"filbot3\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"77964\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/fedoraproject/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/filbot3/48/1769_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> filbot3:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Which mailing lists do you generally look at?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/devel@lists.fedoraproject.org/\">devel@lists.fedoraproject.org</a> mailing list. However it is a high traffic mailing list and sometimes it is laborious to find old messages. And sometimes it can happen that packagers don’t announce their intent to step down.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-03-08T22:32:55.978Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 17, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 153.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77964, "topic_slug": "unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already", "display_username": "Alessio", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/devel@lists.fedoraproject.org/", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "devel - Fedora Mailing-Lists", "clicks": 4}], "read": true, "user_title": "Speak Up!", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 2993, "username": "marcomeyer", "name": "Marco Meyer", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/b193c8/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": true, "admin": false, "staff": true, "user_id": 109, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already/77964/4", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 187440, "name": "Christopher Engelhard", "username": "lcts", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/51a2da/{size}.png", "created_at": "2020-08-18T06:55:15.159Z", "cooked": "<p>When a package is retired from the repositories, the contents of its repository at <a href=\"http://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms\">src.fedoraproject.org/rpms</a> will be replaced by a single file - <code>dead.package</code> - with the reason for retirement. So you should normally be able to look up that reason by looking at the latest commit message (bottom of the package’s page) or contents of the <code>dead.package</code> file. For example, for gitflow the reason is that it had been orphaned for more than 6 weeks, per Fedora policy.</p>\n<p>Miro Hrončok regularly sends mails to the devel@ list listing orphaned packages that are in danger of being retired (<a href=\"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/devel@lists.fedoraproject.org/thread/SISZYZTRO7CG3DWYFYJAMLIKKZG3KO2Q/\">here’s the latest one</a>), so that they can be picked up by other maintainers &amp; important packages don’t fall through the cracks. Those mails would be the best starting point for finding any discussion regarding the <em>retirement</em> of the package.</p>\n<p>The orphaning is unfortunately harder to find, as <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/alciregi\">@alciregi</a> mentioned. The retire-after-6-weeks policy is fairly new, so sometimes packages have been limping along as orphans for a very long time (gitflow’s most recent actual packager commit was 6 years ago, so who knows when it became an orphan or if that was announced to the mailing list …).</p>\n<p>Maintaining the myriad packages in Fedora’s repos takes a lot of time &amp; effort, so unfortunately, if nothing depends on a orphaned package, it isn’t very popular and no maintainer has any personal interest in the software, the package will often end up being retired.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2020-08-18T06:55:15.159Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 28, "reads": 40, "readers_count": 39, "score": 298.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77964, "topic_slug": "unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already", "display_username": "Christopher Engelhard", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "http://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 16}, {"url": "https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/devel@lists.fedoraproject.org/thread/SISZYZTRO7CG3DWYFYJAMLIKKZG3KO2Q/", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Orphaned packages looking for new maintainers - devel - Fedora Mailing-Lists", "clicks": 5}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 6}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 2078, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [{"id": 109, "username": "alciregi", "name": "Alessio", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/alciregi/{size}/5506_2.png"}], "post_url": "/t/unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already/77964/5", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 6}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 6, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 181431, "name": "Richard Shaw", "username": "hobbes1069", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/hobbes1069/{size}/234_2.png", "created_at": "2020-08-24T12:46:30.193Z", "cooked": "<p>Assuming this is the correct upstream, there hasn’t been a commit in 8 years. No code is perfect so I would considered that a dead upstream…</p>\n<aside class=\"onebox allowlistedgeneric\">\n  <header class=\"source\">\n      <img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/favicons/favicon.svg\" class=\"site-icon\" width=\"32\" height=\"32\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/nvie/gitflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">GitHub</a>\n  </header>\n  <article class=\"onebox-body\">\n    <img src=\"https://global.discourse-cdn.com/business4/uploads/askfedora/original/2X/b/bdc7d9eda3a584091703309254fde79cbdd542e8.jpeg\" class=\"thumbnail onebox-avatar\" width=\"400\" height=\"400\">\n\n<h3><a href=\"https://github.com/nvie/gitflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">nvie/gitflow</a></h3>\n\n<p>Git extensions to provide high-level repository operations for Vincent Driessen's branching model. - nvie/gitflow</p>\n\n\n  </article>\n  <div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n    \n    \n  </div>\n  <div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n\n<p>Thanks,<br>\nRichard</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-03-08T07:55:20.336Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 50, "reads": 36, "readers_count": 35, "score": 277.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77964, "topic_slug": "unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already", "display_username": "Richard Shaw", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://github.com/nvie/gitflow", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "GitHub - nvie/gitflow: Git extensions to provide high-level repository operations for Vincent Driessen's branching model.", "clicks": 193}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 246, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already/77964/6", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 188779, "name": "Giacomo Furlan", "username": "elegos", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/elegos/{size}/16487_2.png", "created_at": "2020-10-22T11:37:10.477Z", "cooked": "<p>I’m sorry to necro-reply, but I’ve got updates.</p>\n<p><a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/hobbes1069\">@hobbes1069</a> a code which hasn’t changed since 8 years doesn’t mean it’s outdated, git flow is still used by thousands of people out there <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>BTW I’ve created a COPR repo to easily install git flow in Fedora 31+:<br>\n<a href=\"https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/elegos/gitflow/\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/elegos/gitflow/</a></p>\n<p>It is based upon <a href=\"https://github.com/nvie/gitflow/wiki/Linux#other-linuxes\" class=\"inline-onebox\">Linux · nvie/gitflow Wiki · GitHub</a> - the main difference is that you can uninstall via dnf, instead of using the same install script.</p>\n<p>Cheers</p>\n<p>P.S.<br>\nNext version will use the AVH edition, just saw it now</p>\n<p>Edit: version 1.12.3 is out <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-03-08T07:58:16.811Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 60, "reads": 27, "readers_count": 26, "score": 335.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77964, "topic_slug": "unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already", "display_username": "Giacomo Furlan", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://copr.fedorainfracloud.org/coprs/elegos/gitflow/", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "elegos/gitflow Copr", "clicks": 288}, {"url": "https://github.com/nvie/gitflow/wiki/Linux#other-linuxes", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Linux · nvie/gitflow Wiki · GitHub", "clicks": 147}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": -1, "username": "system", "name": "system", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/system/{size}/2604_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 9719, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [{"id": 246, "username": "hobbes1069", "name": "Richard Shaw", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/hobbes1069/{size}/234_2.png"}], "post_url": "/t/unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already/77964/7", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 110764, "name": "Richard Shaw", "username": "hobbes1069", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/hobbes1069/{size}/234_2.png", "created_at": "2020-10-22T13:59:58.024Z", "cooked": "<p>Well, what I mean is that in general, 8 years is a long time without any commits. If this project was C++ based, that would be like 4 major releases? We technically incorrectly call it “bit rot”, it’s not that the code rotts, but as the compiler gets smarter about finding errors in code it can make it very difficult to maintain.</p>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 8, "updated_at": "2023-03-08T07:28:15.387Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 13, "reads": 26, "readers_count": 25, "score": 70.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 77964, "topic_slug": "unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already", "display_username": "Richard Shaw", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 246, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/unable-to-install-gitflow-on-fedora-32-with-rpm-fusion-enabled-already/77964/8", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}], "stream": [168620, 170414, 141832, 110778, 187440, 181431, 188779, 110764]}, "timeline_lookup": [[1, 2270], [3, 2269], [6, 2263], [7, 2204]], "suggested_topics": [], "tags": [{"id": 365, "name": "f32", "slug": "f32"}, {"id": 878, "name": "dnf", "slug": "dnf"}], "tags_descriptions": {}, "fancy_title": "Unable to install gitflow on Fedora 32 with RPM Fusion enabled already", "id": 77964, "title": "Unable to install gitflow on Fedora 32 with RPM Fusion enabled already", "posts_count": 8, "created_at": "2020-08-17T18:34:43.846Z", 